Sophie: I like joining clubs where people share my interests. Last term I joined the drama club.
Tom: That sounds fun. I usually make friends online first, and then meet them later.
Sophie: Really? Isn''t that a little risky?
Tom: It can be, so I am always careful and never share private information at first.
Sophie: That''s wise. For me, talking face to face feels more real.
Tom: I understand. Maybe the best way is to use both.
Sophie: I agree. What matters most is being honest and kind.', 'Tom 问 Sophie 怎样交新朋友;Sophie 喜欢参加兴趣相投的社团,上学期加入了戏剧社;Tom 则常先在网上交友再见面;Sophie 觉得有点冒险;Tom 说会小心、起初不透露私人信息;Sophie 更喜欢面对面;两人都认为最重要的是真诚和善良。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How does Sophie like to make friends?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["By joining clubs that match her interests.","By writing letters to strangers.","By never leaving her home.","By posting photos of money."]},{"q":"Which club did Sophie join last term?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The football club.","The drama club.","The cooking club.","The chess club."]},{"q":"How does Tom usually make friends?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He meets them online first, then in person.","He never makes new friends.","He only meets them at family parties.","He asks his teacher to choose."]},{"q":"What does Tom do to stay safe online?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He shares his home address at once.","He never shares private information at first.","He gives money to strangers.","He tells everyone his secrets."]},{"q":"What do both speakers agree matters most?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Being rich and famous.","Winning every argument.","Being honest and kind.","Having the newest phone."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
The most common way was to write letters, which could take weeks to arrive.
Later, the telephone made it faster to hear a friend''s voice.
Today, social media and video calls let us talk to faraway friends in seconds.
Yet no matter how the tools change, the wish to stay close to our friends stays the same.', '很久以前,异地的朋友几乎没有保持联系的办法;最常见的是写信,要好几周才到;后来电话让人能更快听到朋友的声音;如今社交媒体和视频通话让我们几秒就能和远方朋友交谈;但无论工具怎么变,想与朋友亲近的愿望始终不变。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Long ago, what was the most common way to keep in touch?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Sending video calls.","Using social media.","Meeting every day.","Writing letters."]},{"q":"What was a problem with that old way?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Letters could take weeks to arrive.","It was too loud.","It needed wi-fi.","It cost nothing at all."]},{"q":"What did the telephone make possible?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Reading old letters.","Hearing a friend''s voice more quickly.","Drawing pictures.","Sending photos by post."]},{"q":"What lets us talk to faraway friends in seconds today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Paper letters.","Walking to their house.","Social media and video calls.","Waiting for weeks."]},{"q":"What stays the same no matter how the tools change?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The price of stamps.","The speed of letters.","The shape of phones.","The wish to stay close to our friends."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Mia: Great idea! She loves music, so how about a small party with her favourite songs?
Ben: Perfect. I can bring a cake. Could you invite her close friends?
Mia: Sure. Let''s keep it a secret so she is really surprised.
Ben: Good thinking. Where should we have it?
Mia: How about the school garden after class? It''s quiet there.
Ben: That works. Let''s tell everyone to arrive before she does.
Mia: Agreed. This is going to be the best birthday surprise ever!', 'Ben 提议为下周五过生日的 Emma 准备惊喜;Mia 赞成,提议办个放她喜欢歌曲的小派对;Ben 负责带蛋糕,请 Mia 邀请她的好友;两人决定保密好让她惊喜;地点定在放学后安静的学校花园;让大家在她到之前先到;期待这是最棒的生日惊喜。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Whose birthday are they planning for?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Emma''s.","Ben''s.","Mia''s.","The teacher''s."]},{"q":"What does Emma love, according to Mia?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Football.","Music.","Painting.","Fishing."]},{"q":"What will Ben bring to the party?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A guitar.","A football.","A cake.","A camera."]},{"q":"Where will they hold the surprise?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["At the train station.","In a shop.","On a boat.","In the school garden."]},{"q":"Why should everyone arrive before Emma?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To keep the party a surprise.","To buy tickets.","To clean the room.","To finish homework."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
First, stay in touch often, even with just a short message.
Second, listen carefully when your friend has a problem, instead of only talking about yourself.
Third, be honest, but always be kind.
And when you make a mistake, say sorry quickly, because a friendship that is cared for can last a lifetime.', '交朋友容易,但维系友谊需要双方努力;第一,常联系,哪怕只是一条短消息;第二,朋友有烦恼时认真倾听,而不是只谈自己;第三,要诚实,但永远要善良;犯错时尽快道歉,因为用心呵护的友谊能维持一生。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"According to the talk, what takes effort from both sides?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Spending money.","Keeping a friendship alive.","Winning games.","Making enemies."]},{"q":"What is the first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Never speak to your friend.","Move far away.","Stay in touch often.","Forget their birthday."]},{"q":"What should you do when your friend has a problem?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only talk about yourself.","Walk away at once.","Laugh at them.","Listen carefully."]},{"q":"What should you do after making a mistake?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Say sorry quickly.","Blame your friend.","Pretend nothing happened.","Stop being friends."]},{"q":"What can a well-cared-for friendship do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["End very soon.","Last a lifetime.","Cause many problems.","Cost a lot of money."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Jack: My best friend is moving to another city next month. I''m afraid we''ll lose touch.
Lucy: I understand. But these days it''s easy to stay in touch online.
Jack: That''s true. We could video-call every weekend.
Lucy: Exactly. And you can still share photos and messages every day.
Jack: You''re right. Maybe distance doesn''t have to end a friendship.
Lucy: It doesn''t. Real friends stay close, however far apart they live.
Jack: Thanks, Lucy. I feel much better now.', 'Lucy 见 Jack 发愁;Jack 说最好的朋友下个月要搬到别的城市,担心会失去联系;Lucy 说如今上网很容易保持联系;Jack 想到可以每周末视频通话;Lucy 说还能每天分享照片和消息;Jack 明白距离不必终结友谊;Lucy 说真朋友无论隔多远都会亲密如初;Jack 道谢,心情好多了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why is Jack worried?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He lost his homework.","He failed an exam.","His best friend is moving away.","He broke his phone."]},{"q":"What is Jack afraid will happen?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He will move house.","He will fail school.","He will lose his money.","They will lose touch."]},{"q":"What does Lucy suggest they do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Stay in touch online.","Stop being friends.","Forget each other.","Never speak again."]},{"q":"How often does Jack think they could video-call?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Once a year.","Every weekend.","Never.","Only on his birthday."]},{"q":"What does Lucy say about real friends?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They forget each other quickly.","They only meet at school.","They stay close however far apart they live.","They argue all the time."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
It means that a true friend is the one who helps you when you are in trouble, not only when life is easy.
Anyone can be there for the good times.
But the friends who stay by your side during hard days are the ones worth keeping.
So when a friend needs you, do not turn away; be the friend you would want to have.', '有句老话:患难见真情;意思是真正的朋友是在你有难时帮你的人,而不只是顺境时;顺境时谁都能陪你;但在艰难日子里仍守在你身边的朋友才值得珍惜;所以当朋友需要你时,别转身离开,要做你自己也希望拥有的那种朋友。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the saying ''a friend in need is a friend indeed'' mean?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Friends should never meet.","Friends only matter when you are rich.","Real friends always argue.","A true friend helps you when you are in trouble."]},{"q":"Who can be there during the good times, according to the talk?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Almost anyone.","Only your teacher.","Nobody at all.","Only your family."]},{"q":"Which friends are worth keeping?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Those who only come to parties.","Those who stay by you during hard days.","Those who never call you.","Those who live nearby only."]},{"q":"What should you do when a friend needs you?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Turn away at once.","Ask for money.","Not turn away; help them.","Tell their secrets."]},{"q":"What does the speaker tell you to be?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The richest person.","The loudest in class.","The first to leave.","The kind of friend you would want to have."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U4', 'fltrp');

